{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016TminCtZBoTaR1SuFef9FS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Checklist for `true-bdd scen check [scenario-id...]`.\n2\t#\n3\t# One cell per (scenario, prompt): each prompt reads ONE registry entry\n4\t# and rules on it alone. scen check is the verifier: a bare run exits 1\n5\t# when any scenario fails a prompt, so it gates a change, and every\n6\t# prompt carries an `F:`, so `--fix` walks the whole checklist.\n7\t#\n8\t# term_closure holds a scenario's words to the documents that define\n9\t# them. Its five code Qs are answered by the engine's own checks,\n10\t# with no AI turn, in their written positions. A failure skips nothing.\n11\t# Their fixes write the product or the\n12\t# architecture document, never the scenario. The four concept checks\n13\t# pass every scenario of a host whose product document declares no\n14\t# concepts as \"not checked\". The public-interface check holds every\n15\t# Scenario to its service declaration.\n16\t#\n17\t# scenario_quality holds the eight questions of the `us-refine`\n18\t# acceptance-criteria checklist that still mean something applied to a\n19\t# single scenario; its fixes rewrite the scenario's own registry entry.\n20\t# The four it dropped threshold over a set (AC count 3-7, at least one\n21\t# happy path, at least two error scenarios, at least 80% convertible).\n22\t\n23\tversion: \"1.0\"\n24\tlast_updated: \"2026-10-21\"\n25\tsections:\n26\t    - id: scenario_quality\n27\t      name: \"Scenario Quality\"\n28\t      description: \"Every registry scenario must read as one testable behaviour, in the product's vocabulary.\"\n29\t      validation_prompts:\n30\t        - Q:\n31\t            prompt: |\n32\t                Decide whether this scenario's steps carry all three\n33\t                Given/When/Then kinds. A violation is any of:\n34\t                - no given step\n35\t                - no when step\n36\t                - no then step\n37\t\n38\t                Pass when the scenario has at least one step of each kind.\n39\t                Fail when any kind is missing.\n40\t\n41\t                Context: emit one line.\n42\t                  - \"<scenario id>: ok\"\n43\t                  - \"<scenario id>: missing <given|when|then> step\"\n44\t          rationale: \"A scenario missing a kind cannot be executed as written: no precondition, no action, or nothing asserted.\"\n45\t          F: \"Add the missing given, when or then step to this Scenario's registry entry, saying what its description already pins, and asking what the step should set up, do or observe first when the description does not say. Change no other step and not the description.\"\n46\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e19a81f-3ff0-4a47-aaa8-07c5e26f1fc7","uuid":"c257487c-fb53-4ab4-bd55-26b31dc7eea6","timestamp":"2026-11-07T04:29:00.603Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"{{CWD}}/true-bdd/checklists/scen-check.yaml","content":"# Checklist for `true-bdd scen check [scenario-id...]`.\n#\n# One cell per (scenario, prompt): each prompt reads ONE registry entry\n# and rules on it alone. scen check is the verifier: a bare run exits 1\n# when any scenario fails a prompt, so it gates a change, and every\n# prompt carries an `F:`, so `--fix` walks the whole checklist.\n#\n# term_closure holds a scenario's words to the documents that define\n# them. Its five code Qs are answered by the engine's own checks,\n# with no AI turn, in their written positions. A failure skips nothing.\n# Their fixes write the product or the\n# architecture document, never the scenario. The four concept checks\n# pass every scenario of a host whose product document declares no\n# concepts as \"not checked\". The public-interface check holds every\n# Scenario to its service declaration.\n#\n# scenario_quality holds the eight questions of the `us-refine`\n# acceptance-criteria checklist that still mean something applied to a\n# single scenario; its fixes rewrite the scenario's own registry entry.\n# The four it dropped threshold over a set (AC count 3-7, at least one\n# happy path, at least two error scenarios, at least 80% convertible).\n\nversion: \"1.0\"\nlast_updated: \"2026-10-21\"\nsections:\n    - id: scenario_quality\n      name: \"Scenario Quality\"\n      description: \"Every registry scenario must read as one testable behaviour, in the product's vocabulary.\"\n      validation_prompts:\n        - Q:\n            prompt: |\n                Decide whether this scenario's steps carry all three\n                Given/When/Then kinds. A violation is any of:\n                - no given step\n                - no when step\n                - no then step\n\n                Pass when the scenario has at least one step of each kind.\n                Fail when any kind is missing.\n\n                Context: emit one line.\n                  - \"<scenario id>: ok\"\n                  - \"<scenario id>: missing <given|when|then> step\"\n          rationale: \"A scenario missing a kind cannot be executed as written: no precondition, no action, or nothing asserted.\"\n          F: \"Add the missing given, when or then step to this Scenario's registry entry, saying what its description already pins, and asking what the step should set up, do or observe first when the description does not say. Change no other step and not the description.\"\n","numLines":46,"startLine":1,"totalLines":46}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016TminCtZBoTaR1SuFef9FS","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
